What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/dcm/state
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        X20 board port
Description:
                Read the AXI clock rate, actual and initial INFRACFG/MCUSYS DCM
                registers, verified BSP enable states and transition count.
                Root may write "infra 0", "infra 1", "peri 0" or "peri 1"
                to apply the corresponding BSP disable/enable sequence.
                "l2 0/1", "cci 0/1", "fabric 0/1" and "adb400 0/1" control
                the four static MCUSYS groups. "mcusys 0/1" applies all four
                in BSP order. Each command requires a literal 0 or 1.
                These writes exclude concurrent CPU hotplug and verify the
                register fields via firmware. Failed transitions roll back.
                "armcore 1" applies BSP ARMCORE MODE1 (mask 0x7777, value
                0x1111); "armcore 0" clears these fields. Reads include its
                actual value, binding-time snapshot and MODE1 enabled flag.
                ARMCORE access uses the CPUFreq supplier's software mutex,
                hardware semaphore and MCUMIXED bridge read/write sequence.
                MODE2 (WFI/WFE triggering) is not exposed.
                "mem 1" applies BSP MEM/DFS_MEM presets and latch sequences:
                active bus divide 1:1, idle divide 1:32, DRAMC free clock 1:1.
                "mem 0" applies the BSP disable sequence. Reads include both
                current values, binding-time snapshots and mem_enabled.
                Initial latch bits must be clear before applying defaults;
                a transition with either latch bit set returns EBUSY.
                Unload/rollback re-latches saved fields before restoring the
                latch selector, and preserves other shared register fields.
                Invalid commands return EINVAL without changing registers.
                The shared TOP_DCMCTL ratio enable stays set while bound.
                Removing the driver restores its original register fields.
                memory_transition_pending reports an outstanding SPM memory
                transaction. MEM writes return EBUSY while it is set. Once
                the memory controller is quiescent, the shared transaction
                API re-latches the pre-transition user settings and clears
                the pending state. The DCM commands themselves do not change
                CPU sync DCM, PLLs, OPPs or DDR PHY frequencies.
